USC: keep the instruction before a mutex release inside the lock

ComputeMutexLockDependence made the release depend on the instructions after
the lock up to uInst - 2, missing the one right before the release (for an
atomic, its store), which could then be scheduled after it.

diff --git a/tools/intern/usc2/dgraph.c b/tools/intern/usc2/dgraph.c
index 57e3e54..dcc0132 100644
--- a/tools/intern/usc2/dgraph.c
+++ b/tools/intern/usc2/dgraph.c
@@ -1834,7 +1834,7 @@ IMG_VOID ComputeMutexLockDependence(PDGRAPH_STATE psDepState)
 			bLocked = IMG_FALSE;
 			/* To prevent instruction from being moved outside of the lock, set the release
 			 instruction as dependent on every instruction in the lock section */
-			for (++uLockInst; uLockInst < (uInst-1); ++uLockInst)
+			for (++uLockInst; uLockInst < uInst; ++uLockInst)
 				AddDependency(psDepState, uLockInst, uInst);
 
 			/* To prevent instructions from being moved into the lock section,
